  "result": "I fixed it. `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` uses `shlex`, which treats `#` as the start of a comment by default. Everything after a `#` was silently dropped, so `a#b` was cut off at the `#`. I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is kept as an ordinary character, which matches how shells handle a mid-word `#`.\n\nI added a regression test, `test_split_arg_string_hash`, in `tests/test_shell_completion.py`. The full `tests/test_shell_completion.py` file passes (59 tests). I didn't run the rest of the suite and didn't add a `CHANGES.md` entry.",
